 "notes": "Scalar-DM search via Yb optical / Cs microwave clock frequency ratio at NMIJ. Headline result is the limit on the scalar-electron coupling d_me (paper Eq.2: m_e(phi)=m_e(1+d_me phi), phi dimensionless relative to Planck scale, Damour-Donoghue/Arvanitaki convention = canonical d_me; no conversion needed). Curve traced from Fig.4(b), the red Yb/Cs lower boundary of the excluded (shaded) region, extracted by rendering the vector PDF (upperbound.pdf) at 4x and thresholding the saturated-red stroke, taking the bottom edge per column; Yb/Cs text label masked. Log axes calibrated on tick labels. Minimum d_me ~= 1.71e-6 at m_phi ~= 4.7e-22 eV, matching the abstract/text quote 'd_me <~ 1.6e-6 at m_phi ~ 5e-22 eV'. Curve spans m_phi ~1.6e-22 to 2e-19 eV as plotted (paper states new best limits over 1e-22 to 1e-20 eV; beyond ~1e-20 Yb/Cs is weaker than Si/H but still the paper's own measured curve). Plotted limits already include the factor-3.0 rescaling the paper applies for scalar-field oscillation interference. rho_DM = 0.3 GeV/cm^3 assumed (Eq.5). 95% CL.",
